  '<p class="gd-p">Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-invoices" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner invoices</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Invoices</b> tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner&#39;s and each application&#39;s Invoices tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> makes an invoice of any amount for an owner&#39;s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The monthly run and tracker invoices: <b class="gd-ui">Run the monthly invoices</b> issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); <b class="gd-ui">Issue all tracker invoices</b> bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/invoices</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1060"><img src="/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1060"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:22.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.7%;top:35.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-make-edit-and-issue-an-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Make, edit and issue an invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. <b class="gd-ui">Add a line</b> for more.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save as draft</b> to come back to it, or <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b> to send it now. On a draft&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Issue and email</b> sends it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid another way? Press <b class="gd-ui">Already paid outside the platform</b> on the invoice: choose how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or card outside the platform), the date and the reference. A draft is issued without the invoice email first, the payment is recorded, and the owner gets no email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the owner a receipt</b>. To record a smaller or extra payment, press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend email</b> sends the invoice again. <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b> opens it as a PDF.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-correct-an-issued-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct an issued invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b>, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press <b class="gd-ui">Void the invoice</b>. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Already paid? Void the payment first, or press <b class="gd-ui">Credit note</b> for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-the-automatic-debit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The automatic debit</h2><p class="gd-p">The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for payments the bank sends back and owners with no bank debit set up.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Notice day</span><em>Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Debit day</span><em>The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Cleared</span><em>The invoice is paid</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Returned, insufficient funds</span><em>The Late Fee (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST) is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Returned for another reason</span><em>No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Scheduled and processing lists each debit. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b> holds one (a reason is needed).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners lists each owner&#39;s bank debit. Use <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send a notice now</b> or, with no bank debit set up, <b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/920"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="920"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.8%;top:21.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.5%;top:35.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91.5%;top:75.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:94.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:14.4%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.4%;top:89.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Insufficient funds: the Late Fee (5% of the unpaid insurance, plus HST; $50.00 on an invoice with no insurance) is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner&#39;s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task. Any debit missed (returned for another reason, too late to retry, or a retry still waiting) comes off the owner&#39;s next revenue statement by itself: when the statement is built, the invoice goes in arrears (a waiting retry is cancelled) and the statement deducts it. Nothing to do.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner&#39;s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no bank debit set up gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-before-the-debit-day-the-debit-preview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Before the debit day: the Debit preview</h2><p class="gd-p">The top of the Debits tab shows the coming debit day.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Debit preview</b> lists each owner with something to debit: the total, whether a bank debit is set up, whether the notice went, and each invoice in one line: the amount, the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment, late fee), the period and how it was worked out, such as &quot;prorated: 20 of 30 days&quot;. The line opens the invoice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Something looks wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Hold</b> beside the owner and give the reason. Nothing is debited for that owner until you press <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Fee check</b> compares the month&#39;s invoices with each car&#39;s signed terms: no monthly fee on a flat monthly payment, a Turo-Only car, a shareholder&#39;s car or a company car, nothing before the Enrollment Date, and the amount the terms give. It changes nothing: void and reissue an invoice that does not match. Each production deploy prints the same check.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-when-a-debit-can-t-go-ahead" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a debit can&#39;t go ahead</h2><p class="gd-p">You get one email: &quot;Can&#39;t collect $X from the owner: the reason&quot;. The reasons are the words of the owner guide: no bank debit set up, owner cancelled the debit at their bank, amount went up after the notice, the bank sent the payment back. The email lists each amount in one line and has one button that fixes it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b> opens the Debits tab on that owner. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b> again there: the owner gets the email to set up their bank debit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a new notice</b> opens the same place with <b class="gd-ui">Send a new notice</b> for the new amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the invoice</b> opens the invoice to record a payment made another way.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b> tab</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Build all for a month</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Build one</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open each draft. Check it, <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> after a correction, <b class="gd-ui">Preview PDF</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Issue to the owner</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Reissue</b> sends a corrected copy; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> exports it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/400"><img src="/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="400"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:79.9%;top:27.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg" alt="An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-staff-commissions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff commissions</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Commissions</b> tab. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Not earned yet</span><em>The rental is ahead, or not paid in full</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pending approval</span><em>Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>You approved it; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded the payment; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Reversed</span><em>Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">By person shows each staff member&#39;s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Prices to review</b> lists prices typed by hand; <b class="gd-ui">Sourcing claims</b> lists staff who say they sourced a website request; <b class="gd-ui">Payments made</b> lists each payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Owner requests</b> lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company&#39;s share or of the cars&#39; rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change and approve</b> (your terms, with a note) or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner&#39;s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner&#39;s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced an owner: the owner&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Sourced by</b>. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month&#39;s rentals</td></tr><tr><td>An owner a salesperson brought in</td><td>The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars&#39;, a partner&#39;s or a shareholder&#39;s cars</td></tr><tr><td>Field staff</td><td>10% (also the field referral fee). Customer service, Fleet and Finance staff get no sales credit or commission, ever: their help is credited as Helped by on the booking and on their scorecard</td></tr><tr><td>Base</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off</td></tr><tr><td>On the owner statement</td><td>An owner&#39;s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner&#39;s car: from CarmaCars&#39; commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month&#39;s Sales tier) goes on the owner&#39;s next statement as an adjustment line.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-field-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Field pay</b> tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Clocked in and out</span><em>Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pay run started</span><em>Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>The figures are frozen, the period&#39;s hours are locked, the statements are numbered</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tab <b class="gd-ui">Pay run</b> shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings &gt; Program, Field pay). <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">After the period ends, press <b class="gd-ui">Start the payroll</b>: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). <b class="gd-ui">Refresh the figures</b> takes in a change made since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The period&#39;s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (<b class="gd-ui">Send again</b> repeats it). The statement&#39;s number opens its PDF; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> gives the run for your accountant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> lists everyone&#39;s shifts of the period. <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hourly rates</b> shows each person&#39;s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with <b class="gd-ui">Set the rate</b> (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Field pay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Overtime</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate</td></tr><tr><td>Vacation pay</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement</td></tr><tr><td>Deductions</td><td>None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer&#39;s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions that net to nothing</td><td>A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-model" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company model</h2><p class="gd-p">Money &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company model</b> is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b>: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months&#39; EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Actuals</b>: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental&#39;s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. <b class="gd-ui">Refresh actuals now</b> recomputes them at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pro forma 5 years</b>: each year&#39;s income statement, cash flow and key figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Assumptions</b>: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the assumptions</b>; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked &quot;From the actuals&quot; left blank uses the latest complete month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download as Excel</b>: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month&#39;s costs in Money &gt; Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-payroll-for-everyone-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payroll for everyone (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payroll</b> is one run every two weeks for the field staff (hours) and for customer service, Fleet and Finance (salary).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A salaried person is paid their monthly salary x 12 / 26, for the days they were employed in the period. The salary is their own (<b class="gd-ui">Set the salary</b>, with a reason), else the monthly pay they were hired at, else their role&#39;s (Program settings, va_salary_defaults), in US dollars unless set otherwise.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Finance prepares it: <b class="gd-ui">Start the payroll</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add a bonus or deduction</b> with the reason, then <b class="gd-ui">Send for approval</b>. You get an alert.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Record all payments</b> (one method and reference; each stub number is added to it) or <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> line by line. Each person gets their stub by email and in their portal.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Admin &gt; Team also has <b class="gd-ui">Schedules</b> (each role&#39;s days and hours, anyone&#39;s own, who is late today) and <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> (every staff member&#39;s KPIs for a week against the targets in Program settings).</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The townhall page: pick the craziest story, enter the week&#39;s social media figures, add the recording link, and mark anyone present or absent. Staff who miss two townhalls in a row are locked until you press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b> on the staff list.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Meetings, on the townhall page, lists the last eight townhalls and the next four. A townhall nobody attended is recorded as not held and counts nobody absent. <b class="gd-ui">This townhall did not happen</b> does the same for a past one (its absences and alerts are cleared, and a lockout it caused is lifted). <b class="gd-ui">Cancel this townhall</b> on an upcoming one sends no reminders for it; <b class="gd-ui">Put it back on</b> undoes that.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each renter and lead shows an Intent card (hot, warm or cold, with the budget, car, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage they mentioned). The live map shows it on each pin. An AI reading fills the gaps within the free daily allowance only (Program settings, intent_ai_enabled).</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Investors see Search traction under the deck: Google clicks and impressions of the last 28 days, indexed pages and the weekly trend. Type the indexed pages from Search Console on the investor deck page under Investors (no API exists for it).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Monthly statements</b> tab: CarmaCars&#39; own monthly statement, in twelve sections.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Download <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b>, <b class="gd-ui">PDF by owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">PDF by vehicle</b>, or press <b class="gd-ui">Email me the PDFs</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Finalize</b> freezes the month. <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> works until then.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/reports</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:28%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.4%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.1%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.9%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from the revenue statement</h3><p class="gd-p">On an owner&#39;s page, the <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b> button sets <b class="gd-ui">How fees are paid</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit</b> (the default) or <b class="gd-ui">Take from revenue statement</b>. Taken from the statement, the owner&#39;s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;. Approved, the invoice reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task <b class="gd-ui">Invoice ... back to the bank debit</b>.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The flat-rate agreements</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b> instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner&#39;s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK</b> is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-how-it-s-paid-bank-debit-or-deducted-from-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How it&#39;s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit on the 15th</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> (taken from the owner&#39;s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On an invoice, <b class="gd-ui">How it&#39;s paid</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For the first and last month, choose <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> on the Terms tab (or at approval).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the Terms tab, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the agreed one-off fees</b> makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner&#39;s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-referral-links-between-owners-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Referral links between owners (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">When one owner referred another, open the referrer&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Referral links</b>, <b class="gd-ui">This owner referred another owner</b>: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner&#39;s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a <b class="gd-ui">Referral share</b> line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars&#39; share, never the referred owner&#39;s payout. With <b class="gd-ui">sees the cars</b> on, the referrer finds <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner&#39;s details. <b class="gd-ui">End</b> stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-statement-periods-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statement periods (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Statements run from the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th covers them. A rental that crosses the cutoff, or a long weekly or biweekly rental, is paid for the days inside each period, never twice. Each statement lists amounts still uncollected from the renter separately; they are paid on the statement after they are collected.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-the-owner-forecast-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The owner forecast (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Each owner sees a <b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b> on their Home: the next 12 months of each car, projected occupancy and projected owner revenue (before fees). Open an owner in <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>: the <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> shows the same <b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every car starts from the GTA seasonal curve: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owner forecast: the GTA seasonal curve</b> (a factor for each month, jan to dec, 1.00 is an average month) and <b class="gd-ui">Owner forecast: the occupancy of an average month</b> (60% by default). A month&#39;s curve is the average month times its factor.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Once a car has 3 full months on the program, its own occupancy is blended in: its own level (each month&#39;s occupancy divided by that month&#39;s factor) times the month&#39;s factor, weighted half after 3 months, two thirds after 6, four fifths after 12. The season always stays in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Bookings hidden from the owner (an insurer replacement hidden from them, or one never shown), test bookings and the owner&#39;s own trips are not counted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Projected owner revenue: occupancy times the days of the month times the car&#39;s owner revenue per booked day, from its own statements of the last 12 months, else its daily rate less the Revenue Share.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Every owner statement (the owner&#39;s page, yours and the PDF) has a <b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b> line: next month against the statement&#39;s month, higher or lower, by how many points and about how much owner revenue, and why (the season).</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Change a factor when the season moves (a big event, a new airport route): every owner&#39;s forecast follows on their next visit.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-use-charges-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner-use charges (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The charges of a booking an owner makes of their own car (for themselves or for someone else) are billed to the owner by themselves: damage up to the deductible, tickets, tolls, fuel, kilometres, cleaning, smoking, a late return and the other fees. Add them as on any rental (the return, the Money tab); a fee that needs evidence waits for it, as always.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing goes on a renter statement. About 15 minutes after a charge is ready it is put on an owner invoice titled &quot;Charges on your booking&quot;, issued and due the same day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">It is collected in this order: the owner&#39;s card on file at once; with no card, a bank debit started the same day (not the 15th); with no method, or when the charge fails, the owner gets the invoice with the pay link and reminders every 2 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An invoice still unpaid after 7 days, or at the statement cut-off (the 7th) if that comes first, is deducted from the owner&#39;s next statement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The owner gets an email and an alert at each step, listing each charge with its evidence. A failed charge also alerts Admins.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab shows <b class="gd-ui">Charges billed to the owner</b>: the charges waiting for evidence, and each invoice with what is open, how it is being collected and the day it would be deducted from the statement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The days are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner-use charges and the Late Fee on unpaid insurance</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-late-fee-on-unpaid-insurance-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Late Fee on unpaid insurance (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s Late Fee on insurance is 5% of the unpaid insurance of the invoice (it was $50 per vehicle). It is added once, as its own line, when the debit of the 15th fails or the invoice is unpaid the day after its due date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The fee carries HST by default (it is a penalty, not insurance; insurance itself has none). Ask the accountant; the switch is in Program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The unpaid insurance and the fee are deducted from the owner&#39;s next statement by themselves, as two lines: the invoice, and &quot;Late Fee, invoice INV-n&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The owner is reminded 3 days before the due date and told when the fee is added. An invoice with no insurance on it keeps the flat Late Fee.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The updated owner agreement (4.4 and Schedule B) is published for owners to accept (it is listed with the other terms under Settings), without signing again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-finance-dashboard-and-the-bank-release-49" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Company</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Finance</b> (the first tab of Company; Finance has the same page under <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Finance</b>) is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cash position</b>: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe&#39;s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and <b class="gd-ui">Free cash</b>: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week&#39;s download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money in</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Money out</b> for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Held for others</b>: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">HST</b> for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter balances overdue</b> (past the statement&#39;s 7 days) and <b class="gd-ui">Insurer invoices unpaid</b> by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Twelve months</b>: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement&#39;s net where one is built.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bank lines</b> is the reconciliation:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In RBC online banking open the account, <b class="gd-ui">Download transactions</b>, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on <b class="gd-ui">Import from RBC online banking</b>. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">No match</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b> a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'finance', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-requests', 'You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips. There is no commission for Finance, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. **Money** opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: **To handle** (payments, deposits, refunds), **By day** (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), **All payments**, **Refunds**, **Deposits**, **Reconciliation** and **Unlinked Stripe** (the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, checked every night, with a best guess of the booking: an Admin links one from the booking''s Money tab; put one aside with the reason when it is not a booking''s payment). **Owner money** lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.

## Your queue

Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.

![The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.](/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 20.3 24.3")

## Payments by day

**Money**, the **By day** tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.

1. Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.
3. At the end of the day count the drawer and press **Record the count**. The difference shows "balanced", or "over" or "short" with the amount.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.

## Payments, deposits, refunds

**Money**, the **To handle** tab.

1. Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank''s reason.
2. Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.
3. Refunds in progress. Press **Request the refund** and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then **Issue the refund**.
4. Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 865; address: carmacars.ca/va/money; pins: 1 10.6 60.3, 2 72.4 21.6, 3 73.2 33.8, 4 11.0 45.9")

## A payment received another way

An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.

1. Owner invoice: on **Payments, deposits, refunds**, find it under Owner invoices owing and press **Record payment**.
2. Renter: beside the failed payment, press **Paid another way**. Or open the booking''s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.
3. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.
4. Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press **Record payment**.

The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.

Each month''s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.


A pay link for the rental, the fees or the balance asks for what is owed and never more (release 48): the booking''s total less every payment of it, refunds counted back. After a change to the total, the link is for the difference. A booking paid in full gets no balance link: anything on top is a later charge, with its reason. A new link replaces any open one for the booking''s money, and a link still open when a payment lands is cancelled by itself (the booking history says so), so the renter is never charged twice.
## Cards, holds and deposits given back

On the booking''s Money tab.

1. After the return, **Charge the renter**: the Reason from the list (Other with its note), the Amount, and the line that says where the money comes from (the deposit hold while it is valid, else the card on file, else a pay link) before you press **Charge $...**. Before the return, Rental charges, **A later charge**, with the same reason list on the renter''s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, **Charge the card on file as the deposit**.
2. A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list (the rest is released), or **Release**. **Hold expired**: nothing can be kept from it; press **Charge the card on file instead** (the amount and the reason are filled in). While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.
3. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

## Settle a deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (**Keep the whole deposit (damage)**) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## Read a toll notice

1. Open **Tolls and tickets** and press **Read a notice**.
2. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.
3. Press **Read it**. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.
4. Press **Checked against the notice** on each line (**Leave out** to skip one), then **Save as checked** and **Confirm and import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read; pins: 2 19.5 44.1, 3 4.1 64.8, 4 4.1 89.7")

> Tip: In the work queue, **Match again** retries the match after a fix, and **Dispute** marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.

![The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice''s plate, date, amount and match.](/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls; pins: 1 23.6 12.2")

## Reconciliation and Turo trips

1. **Money**, the **Reconciliation** tab: press **Record a processor payout**, then **Match** it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.
2. **Turo trips**: press **Add a trip** for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press **Import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/turo; pins: 2 95.1 14.8")

## Deposits to release

A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: "Release the deposit for" the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.

1. Open the task: it opens the booking''s **Money** tab.
2. Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.
3. The task closes by itself once nothing is left to give back.

### Card payments outside the site and the card reader
On a booking''s **Money** tab: **Record card payment** records a card taken in the Stripe Dashboard or on a reader (the last 4 digits always; a Stripe payment id, pi_..., checks it, and a deposit hold needs it). **Charge on reader** and **Hold deposit on reader** send the amount to the S700; the renter taps the card and the screen updates by itself. On a credit card coverage rental the whole rental is paid on the same card: another card is refused with the reason, and only an Admin can allow another one.

## Deposit holds and partner invoices (release 28)

Deposits stay as holds with Stripe and are never captured by itself. A job re-authorizes a hold by itself about 24 hours before it expires; when it cannot, you get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**. A **The deposit hold expires soon** To do opens the booking: **Re-authorize the hold** places a new hold on the saved card and releases the old one; or **Keep part (damage/fees)** for only what is owed. A deposit not taken yet: in the Security deposit panel, **Hold on the card on file**. Under **Money** > **Partner invoices** you write invoices to body shops, tow trucks and storage yards for their kickback, send them, record the cheques and e-Transfers that come in, and export the CSV for the bookkeeper.

## Kickbacks and repairs

**Money** > **Kickbacks and repairs**: the kickbacks received on partner invoices (before HST) and the repair costs paid by CarmaCars for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV. An invoice with no car counts nowhere until you choose it: open the invoice under **Partner invoices** and press **Choose the car**. Add a repair cost with **Add a repair cost**; Fleet adds them on the car''s page too.

### A debit deposit''s card fee
A deposit charged (not held) on a debit or prepaid card carries the non-refundable **Card processing fee for a debit deposit**, shown on its line in the history and on the receipt. The deposit refund returns the deposit only.

## Partners, the timesheet and ended trips

1. **More finance** > **Partners**: the rental partners (their pages, cars, rates, invoices) and the referral partners (kickbacks, payments), with every action an Admin has there.
2. **Hours** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked. Add forgotten hours or void a wrong entry, with the reason.
3. **Close ended trips**: mark trips that ended and were never closed, and choose the deposit decision. An Admin presses Release; nothing is released by itself.


## Deposit review: double-check, tolls and tickets, then bill or release

Once Fleet signed every item of a returned booking you get a To do to double-check the deposit review. The deposit stays held until you signed every item too; only an Admin can release it earlier, with the reason.

1. Open **Money** > **Deposit reviews** and open the booking.
2. Press **Double-check** on each item: read Fleet''s finding and the photos, then **OK** or **Issue** with the amount to bill. Someone else double-checks an item you signed for Fleet.
3. **Highway tolls**: open the toll operator''s site from the review, search the plate for the rental dates, then double-check the item.
4. **Tickets**: open each place in the list (its official lookup link), search the plate, and press **None found** or **A ticket**. A ticket is logged in **Tolls and tickets** with the place and the plate and matched to the booking there. The Tickets item waits until every place is checked.
5. Then open **Money** on the booking: bill what is owed with the charge after the return, or release the deposit.

### The sweep, Monday, Wednesday and Friday
On each sweep day a To do **Deposit check sweep** lists every plate returned since the last sweep and every booking still inside the toll and ticket window. **Deposit reviews** > **This sweep** shows them by plate with every link, so you check them in one go. The days are in Program settings.

### Countdowns
**Money** > **Countdowns** (and the top of **To handle**, and each booking) shows the time left before each deposit hold expires (with when the automatic re-authorization runs, 24 hours before), before each deposit is due back to the renter, and before the next payment of a weekly, biweekly or monthly plan. Red is within 24 hours or late, amber within 48. Sort by any column. You get an alert at 48 and 24 hours, and the counts are in your morning digest.

### Do sales too
Under **My numbers** > **Do sales too**, press **I want to do sales too**: the Sales path is added to your academy (your Finance work is never held by it), and the Sales pages open once you pass it.


## The fuel line on the deposit review (release 35)

The fuel item shows **Suggested** with its working: the tank x the fuel missing x the pump price x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee. It is a line on the return charges, never charged by itself: sign the item, then bill it with the rest from the booking''s Money. A pump receipt still wins: enter it when the car was filled up.

## Statements and payroll (release 35)

- Statements cover the 8th to the 7th, paid on the 10th; amounts not yet collected from the renter are listed apart and paid on the statement after they come in.
- Payroll every two weeks: prepare the run with any bonus or deduction and its reason, then send it for approval. An Admin approves and records the payments.
- Email: Settings, Usage shows the real daily capacity of our sending services together; nothing to count by hand.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Payments by e-Transfer or cash, deposits and tips

1. **Record a payment**: a payment of the whole total pays every line of the booking (the rental, short notice, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan), whichever part you record it for. When nothing is open, a booking waiting for payment is confirmed by itself.
2. **The deposit by e-Transfer or cash is doubled**: twice the car''s deposit by default (Program settings). The Security deposit card shows both amounts ("Credit card hold $300.00; e-Transfer or cash $600.00 (2x)"), and the renter sees them on the offer and the pay page before paying.
3. **Collect the deposit** > Cash or e-Transfer: leave the amount empty to take what is owed. Less is recorded as a part (the card says **under, still owed $X** and **Collect the $X still owed** takes the rest); more is held and given back with the deposit (**over, to return $X**).
4. **Change the deposit** on Edit booking (an Admin, with the reason), even while the booking waits for payment: the Money tab, the deposit link and Collect $X deposit follow at once.
5. **Voided a deposit by mistake?** After the void the deposit is **Not collected** again everywhere (the header too): record it again.
6. **Tips**: the renter can add one when paying, on the receipt and from the after-trip email. A tip in cash or by e-Transfer: **Tips** > **Record a tip**. Half goes to the booking''s salesperson and half to the staff member at the handover; with no staff salesperson (a direct booking) CarmaCars keeps that half; one person who did both gets it all. An Admin can give one tip another split (**All to ...**, **Back to the usual split**). A tip is never part of the rental or the owner''s share.
7. A greyed-out button says under it what to do first.

## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

1. A fee waiting for its evidence stays off the statement; the rest goes as usual. Issuing a statement with only such a fee says what is missing.
2. A To do in the Finance queue asks for a toll or ticket notice, a receipt or an invoice. Attach it on the Money tab (**Attach evidence**).
3. When the evidence of a held fee arrives after the Check-out statement, you get **Evidence attached: bill the fee that was waiting**: bill it from the Money tab.
4. Only an Admin charges a fee without its evidence, with the reason.', 'Finance', 'Payments, deposits and refunds, tolls and tickets, reconciliation, the Finance dashboard and Turo trips.',
  'You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips. There is no commission for Finance, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. **Money** opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: **To handle** (payments, deposits, refunds), **By day** (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), **All payments**, **Refunds**, **Deposits**, **Reconciliation** and **Unlinked Stripe** (the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, checked every night, with a best guess of the booking: an Admin links one from the booking''s Money tab; put one aside with the reason when it is not a booking''s payment). **Owner money** lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.

## Your queue

Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.

![The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.](/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 20.3 24.3")

## Payments by day

**Money**, the **By day** tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.

1. Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.
3. At the end of the day count the drawer and press **Record the count**. The difference shows "balanced", or "over" or "short" with the amount.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.

## Payments, deposits, refunds

**Money**, the **To handle** tab.

1. Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank''s reason.
2. Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.
3. Refunds in progress. Press **Request the refund** and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then **Issue the refund**.
4. Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.

